{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Et ha-kol.</b> I have recognized that Elohim made everything beautiful in its time: death at the time of old age, and every thing in its time, according to the design of supernal wisdom. And the word עולם in all of Scripture we find only as denoting time and eternity, as in אלהי עולם (God of eternity), like אלהי נצח or אלהי קדם, and likewise ומתחת זרועות עולם. And the sense of גם את העולם נתן בלבם is that human beings busy themselves as though they will live forever, and because of their busying themselves they do not understand the work of Elohim from beginning to end. And there are interpreters who say עולם means this world, as in the language of our earlier Sages, of blessed memory, and the sense is: desire for the world."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:23.588220679Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}